+/// How many slots of a profile may be deep at once.
+///
+/// A `k`-deep profile class has `C(depth, k)` members per sweep step, so the
+/// *old* rule could not afford a deep class on a wide segmentation at all: the
+/// walk was depth-then-breadth and stopped at the reserve, so a class was only
+/// reached once every shallower class had been paid for in full, which made
+/// the class count — not the reserve — the thing that bounded the depth, and
+/// the count is a function of how many slots the segmentation has.
+///
+/// That reason expired with the class *order*.  [`coverage_tuples`] now pays
+/// for the whole of the one-deep classes first, so a reserve smaller than the
+/// number of slots still touches every slot as it always did, and then
+/// interleaves the deeper shapes round by round.  The deepest classes are
+/// funded from the reserve's *second* tuple onwards whatever the class count
+/// is, so what the cap bounds is the depth of a **funded** shape, and nothing
+/// else: it is the ceiling on how many slots a single profile representative
+/// may be off the traversal's best index in, and the class count no longer
+/// bounds it.  Nothing in the search spends per deep slot, so raising the cap
+/// costs no extra emission allowance and no extra pop — the same 16 tuples
+/// are offered, and the extra ones on a deep segmentation are the deepest
+/// classes that were already in the candidate set.
+const EMIT_PROFILE_MAX_DEEP: usize = 4;
+
+/// The per-slot rotation of a profile class's sweep.
+///
+/// A shape class's slots each sweep **their own** candidate list, at their own
+/// width and their own rotation of the phase.  The width is what makes a
+/// coordinate legal in its own slot at all, and the rotation is what makes the
+/// coordinates *independent*: with one shared index per class, two slots of a
+/// class can never hold two different alternatives, so every wording the
+/// reserve emits is a diagonal of its class's index rectangle rather than a
+/// point of it, and a resegmentation — which is deep in several slots at ranks
+/// unrelated to one another — is not late in the reserve's order but absent
+/// from it.
+///
+/// Only non-zero and distinct across the slot indices the search produces is
+/// required, which is what it is for every slot count a run of targets makes
+/// (no segmentation is five slots wide more than once and none is above ten).
+/// A rotation is a shift, so a run of phases still tiles each list; the
+/// offsets between a class's coordinates are what become a function of the
+/// phase, which is the point.
+const COVERAGE_SLOT_ROTATION: usize = 37;
 
